  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Duns">Duns</ref> 1</head>
        <ab type="selectedText" xml:lang="und">Ðæt is: gif man trode bedrifð forstolenes yrfes of stæðe on oðer, ðonne befæste man þæt spo[r] landesmannum oððe mid mearce gecyðe, þæt man riht drife.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en">That is, if a man follows up the track of stolen cattle from one bank to the other [across the river], then he [shall] entrust that trail to the local people or prove with evidence that he is making a legal pursuit.</ab>
        <ab type="supplementaryText" xml:lang="und">Hoc est: si uestigium furati pecoris minetur de loco in locum, tunc committatur ipsum uestigium landhominibus uel cum marca monstretur, quod rectum prosequantur.</ab>
      </div>
    </body>
